  "_changelog": "CHANGE LOG\nField: LocalOperatorNames | Change: removed `SeqRange` | Reason: `SeqRange == ...` is a simple LET-bound name, not a parametric local operator.\nField: SetEnumeration | Change: corrected `{\"t\", \"l\", \"a\", \"p\", \"u\", \"s\"}` to `{\"t\", \"l\", \"a\", \"p\", \"l\", \"u\", \"s\"}` | Reason: JSON entry omitted a literal `\\\"l\\\"`; set expression must match file verbatim.\nField: SetEnumeration | Change: removed `{<<1, 2, 3, 2>>}` | Reason: this set enumeration does not appear anywhere in the TLA+ file.\nField: TupleConstructor | Change: removed `<<\"a\", \"b\"}>` | Reason: invalid/nonexistent tuple expression; does not appear in file.\nField: TupleConstructor | Change: removed duplicate `<<1>>` | Reason: deduplication required.\nField: TupleConstructor | Change: removed duplicate `<<2>>` | Reason: deduplication required.\nField: TupleConstructor | Change: removed duplicate `<<\"a\", \"b\", \"c\">>` | Reason: deduplication required.\nField: TupleConstructor | Change: removed duplicate `<<\"d\", \"d\", \"d\">>` absence by keeping only actual occurrences | Reason: only expressions that literally appear in file should be retained; duplicate/nonessential repeat eliminated in normalized corrected list.\nField: RangeExpr | Change: added `1..5` | Reason: appears in commented TLA+ code as `BoundedSeq(1..5, 5)`; per instruction, read entire file completely and include every distinct range appearing in file.\nField: StringLiterals | Change: added `ab` | Reason: string literal appears in commented test `FlattenSeq(<<\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\">>) = \\\"ab\\\"`; string literals in the file must be captured.\nField: Completeness check | Change: verified top-level operator counts match | Reason: file count = 144, JSON OperatorDefNames count = 144.",
